<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>GB Power Weekly, week ending {{ week_ending_display }} | Mazao Consulting</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --navy:#10294A; --navy-mid:#2B4B73; --ink:#2F3A45; --muted:#6B7783;
    --rule:#D8DEE6; --rule-soft:#EAEEF3; --callout:#F3F7FB; --callout-edge:#C6D6E6;
    --signal:#B04A39; --wind:#5A8F6E; --demand:#8C7BA6; --paper:#FFFFFF;
    --sans:-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,"Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;
    --serif:Georgia,"Iowan Old Style","Times New Roman",serif;
  }
  * { box-sizing:border-box; }
  body {
    margin:0; background:var(--paper); color:var(--ink);
    font-family:var(--sans); font-size:15px; line-height:1.55;
    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
  }
  .wrap { max-width:1060px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 28px 72px; }
  .num { font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; font-feature-settings:"tnum" 1; }

  /* header */
  header { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline;
    gap:24px; flex-wrap:wrap; padding:26px 0 12px; border-bottom:3px solid var(--navy); }
  .brand { font-weight:700; color:var(--navy); letter-spacing:.01em; font-size:17px; }
  .brand span { font-weight:400; color:var(--muted); }
  .stamp { color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; }
  .draft { margin:14px 0 0; padding:9px 14px; background:#FFF6E5;
    border-left:3px solid #C08A2E; font-size:13.5px; color:#6A5220; }

  /* hero */
  h1 { font-family:var(--serif); font-weight:400; color:var(--navy);
    font-size:29px; line-height:1.32; margin:30px 0 6px; max-width:34em; }
  .byline { color:var(--muted); font-size:13.5px; margin:0 0 22px; }

  /* kpis */
  .kpis { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0;
    border-top:1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); margin:26px 0 0; }
  .kpi { padding:16px 20px 15px; border-left:1px solid var(--rule-soft); }
  .kpi:first-child { border-left:0; padding-left:0; }
  .kpi .k { color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; }
  .kpi .v { font-size:27px; color:var(--navy); font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.01em; margin:2px 0 1px; }
  .kpi .v small { font-size:14px; font-weight:500; color:var(--navy-mid); }
  .kpi .ref { font-size:13px; color:var(--muted); }
  .up { color:var(--signal); } .down { color:var(--wind); }

  /* sections */
  h2 { font-size:15px; color:var(--navy); margin:44px 0 4px; font-weight:700; }
  .lede { color:var(--muted); font-size:13.5px; margin:0 0 14px; max-width:66ch; }
  .rule { border:0; border-top:1px solid var(--rule); margin:0; }

  .drivers { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:26px; margin-top:18px; }
  .card h3 { font-size:14px; margin:0 0 2px; color:var(--navy); font-weight:600; }
  .card p { margin:8px 0 0; font-size:13.5px; color:var(--ink); }
  .card .v { font-size:20px; color:var(--navy); font-weight:600; }

  .callout { background:var(--callout); border:1px solid var(--callout-edge);
    padding:14px 18px; margin:16px 0 0; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:15px; color:#22364C; }
  .callout p { margin:0; }

  /* charts */
  svg { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; }
  .grid { stroke:var(--rule-soft); stroke-width:1; }
  .daysep { stroke:var(--rule); stroke-width:1; stroke-dasharray:2 3; }
  .da { fill:none; stroke:var(--navy); stroke-width:1.8; stroke-linejoin:round; }
  .imb { fill:none; stroke:#A9BACB; stroke-width:1; stroke-linejoin:round; }
  .mark { fill:var(--signal); }
  .markline { stroke:var(--signal); stroke-width:1; stroke-dasharray:2 2; }
  .note { font-family:var(--sans); font-size:12px; fill:var(--signal); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .ax { font-family:var(--sans); font-size:12px; fill:var(--muted); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .ax.sm { font-size:10.5px; }
  .unit { fill:var(--navy-mid); }
  .line { fill:none; stroke-width:1.8; } .dot { stroke:none; }
  .w.line, .w.dot { stroke:var(--wind); fill:var(--wind); }
  .w.fill { fill:var(--wind); opacity:.13; }
  .d.line, .d.dot { stroke:var(--demand); fill:var(--demand); }
  .d.fill { fill:var(--demand); opacity:.13; }
  .legend { display:flex; gap:20px; font-size:12.5px; color:var(--muted); margin:10px 0 0; }
  .swatch { display:inline-block; width:16px; height:2.5px; vertical-align:middle; margin-right:6px; }
  .legend span { margin-right:20px; }
  .legend.key .swatch { height:11px; }
  .swatch.pale { outline:1px solid var(--rule); outline-offset:-1px; }

  /* table */
  table { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin-top:14px;
    font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; font-size:14px; }
  /* Day-by-day is 6 columns across a full week -- doesn't shrink below
     its own content's width (standard table layout), so it overflowed
     the page on a phone viewport, confirmed live, same issue as PPA
     Tools' CfD tables (see app.css's own .table-scroll comment there;
     this is a separate, standalone stylesheet so it needs its own
     copy). Scroll it within its own box instead of past the page edge. */
  .table-scroll { overflow-x:auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch; }
  caption { text-align:left; color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; padding-bottom:8px; }
  th, td { padding:9px 10px; text-align:right; border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule-soft); }
  thead th { color:var(--navy); font-weight:600; font-size:12.5px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--navy); }
  tbody th { text-align:left; font-weight:500; color:var(--ink); }
  td.em { color:var(--navy); font-weight:600; }
  tbody tr:last-child th, tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule); }
  .dl { font-size:13px; margin-top:10px; }

  /* deeper */
  .deeper { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); gap:18px; margin-top:16px; }
  .deeper a { display:block; padding:16px 18px; border:1px solid var(--rule);
    text-decoration:none; color:var(--navy); background:var(--paper); }
  .deeper a:hover { border-color:var(--navy-mid); background:var(--callout); }
  .deeper strong { display:block; font-size:14.5px; }
  .deeper span { color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; }
  a { color:var(--navy-mid); }
  a:focus-visible, .deeper a:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--navy); outline-offset:2px; }

  /* footer */
  footer { margin-top:52px; padding-top:16px; border-top:1px solid var(--navy);
    font-size:12.5px; color:var(--muted); }
  footer dl { display:grid; grid-template-columns:150px 1fr; gap:6px 18px; margin:12px 0 0; }
  footer dt { color:var(--ink); } footer dd { margin:0; }

  @media (max-width:820px) {
    .kpis { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr); }
    .kpi:nth-child(3) { border-left:0; padding-left:0; }
    .kpi { border-top:1px solid var(--rule-soft); }
    .kpi:nth-child(-n+2) { border-top:0; }
    .drivers, .deeper { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    h1 { font-size:24px; }
    footer dl { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:2px 0; }
    footer dt { margin-top:8px; }
  }
  @media print {
    .draft, .deeper { display:none; }
    body { font-size:11pt; } .wrap { max-width:none; padding:0; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce) { * { transition:none !important; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<header>
  <div class="brand">Mazao Consulting <span>/ GB Power Weekly</span></div>
  <div class="stamp num">Week ending {{ week_ending_display }} &middot; issued {{ issued_display }}</div>
</header>

<h1>{{ headline }}</h1>
<p class="byline">{{ byline }}</p>

{{ hero_svg }}
<div class="legend">
  <span><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--navy)"></span>Day-ahead</span>
  <span><span class="swatch" style="background:#A9BACB"></span>Imbalance</span>
  <span><span class="swatch" style="background:var(--signal)"></span>Week high</span>
</div>

<div class="kpis">
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="k">Average day-ahead</div>
    <div class="v num">£{{ '%.2f'|format(kpi.avg_day_ahead) }} <small>/MWh</small></div>
    <div class="ref num">{% if kpi.avg_day_ahead_pct_change is not none %}<span class="{{ 'up' if kpi.avg_day_ahead_pct_change >= 0 else 'down' }}">{{ '+' if kpi.avg_day_ahead_pct_change >= 0 else '' }}{{ kpi.avg_day_ahead_pct_change }}%</span> on prior week{% else %}prior week: n/a{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="k">Best 1h spread</div>
    <div class="v num">£{{ '%.2f'|format(kpi.best_spread_week) }} <small>/MWh</small></div>
    <div class="ref num">{% if kpi.spread_30d_median is not none %}30-day median £{{ '%.2f'|format(kpi.spread_30d_median) }}{% else %}30-day median: n/a{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="k">Wind share of generation</div>
    <div class="v num">{{ kpi.wind_share_pct }}<small>%</small></div>
    <div class="ref num">{% if kpi.wind_share_pct_change_pts is not none %}<span class="{{ 'up' if kpi.wind_share_pct_change_pts >= 0 else 'down' }}">{{ '+' if kpi.wind_share_pct_change_pts >= 0 else '' }}{{ kpi.wind_share_pct_change_pts|int }} pts</span> on prior week{% else %}prior week: n/a{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="k">Highest imbalance price</div>
    <div class="v num">£{{ '%.0f'|format(kpi.highest_imbalance_value) }} <small>/MWh</small></div>
    <div class="ref num">{{ kpi.highest_imbalance_day_label }}, SP{{ kpi.highest_imbalance_sp }}</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>What moved the week</h2>
<p class="lede">Three drivers, each with the number that matters.</p>
<hr class="rule">
<div class="drivers">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Wind output</h3>
    {{ wind_spark_svg }}
    <p><span class="v num">{{ drivers.wind.low_gw }} GW</span> daily low on {{ drivers.wind.low_day }},
    against {{ drivers.wind.high_gw }} GW on {{ drivers.wind.high_day }}. {{ driver_notes[0] }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Peak demand</h3>
    {{ demand_spark_svg }}
    <p><span class="v num">{{ drivers.demand.peak_gw }} GW</span> peak on {{ drivers.demand.peak_day }}. {{ driver_notes[1] }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Periods above &pound;100</h3>
    {{ p100_spark_svg }}
    <p><span class="v num">{{ drivers.periods_above_100.high }}</span> settlement periods cleared above £100 on
    {{ drivers.periods_above_100.high_day }}, against {{ drivers.periods_above_100.low }} on {{ drivers.periods_above_100.low_day }}. {{ driver_notes[2] }}</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout">
  <p>Best 1-hour spread of the week: £{{ '%.2f'|format(kpi.best_spread_week) }}/MWh, on {{ kpi.best_spread_week_day }}.
  Wind share of generation was {{ kpi.wind_share_pct }}% across the week.</p>
</div>

<h2>Where value sat in the day</h2>
<p class="lede">Price relative to that day's own average, by settlement period. Blue is below
the daily mean, which is when a battery charges. Red is above it.</p>
<hr class="rule">
{{ heatmap_svg }}
<div class="legend key">
  <span><span class="swatch" style="background:rgb(139,167,207)"></span>&minus;{{ heatmap_scale|int }} £/MWh</span>
  <span><span class="swatch pale" style="background:#EEF2F6"></span>Day mean</span>
  <span><span class="swatch" style="background:rgb(176,76,66)"></span>+{{ heatmap_scale|int }} £/MWh</span>
</div>

<h2>Day by day</h2>
<hr class="rule">
<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
  <caption>Day-ahead prices and best 1-hour battery spread, £/MWh</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr><th scope="col" style="text-align:left">Day</th><th scope="col">Average</th>
    <th scope="col">Peak</th><th scope="col">Trough</th><th scope="col">Best 1h spread</th>
    <th scope="col">Wind share</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for d in days %}
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">{{ d.label }}</th>
      <td>{{ '%.2f'|format(d.day_ahead_avg) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(d.day_ahead_peak) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(d.day_ahead_trough) }}</td>
      <td class="em">{{ '%.2f'|format(d.best_spread) }}</td><td>{{ d.wind_share_pct|round|int if d.wind_share_pct is not none else 'n/a' }}%</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="dl"><a href="#">Download this week as CSV</a></p>

<h2>Go deeper</h2>
<hr class="rule">
<div class="deeper">
  <a href="/bess"><strong>BESS analytics</strong><span>Ancillary service and Balancing Mechanism activity by participant</span></a>
  <a href="/live"><strong>Live market</strong><span>Current prices, margin and imbalance</span></a>
  <a href="/ppa"><strong>PPA tools</strong><span>Shape, capture rate and pricing support</span></a>
</div>

<footer>
  <strong>Data, assumptions and limits</strong>
  <dl>
    <dt>Sources</dt><dd>Elexon Insights (MID, DISEBSP, FUELHH, INDO). Day-ahead reference is Elexon's Market Index Data, volume-weighted across reporting providers.</dd>
    <dt>Time basis</dt><dd>Settlement periods 1 to 48, Europe/London. Clock-change days carry 46 or 50 periods.</dd>
    <dt>Data vintage</dt><dd>{{ run_basis }} Extracted {{ extracted_display }}.</dd>
    {% if day_ahead_gaps %}
    <dt>Day-ahead coverage</dt><dd>{% for g in day_ahead_gaps %}{{ g.date }}: {{ g.expected - g.missing_periods|length }} of {{ g.expected }} periods ({{ g.missing_periods|length }} had no priced trade from either MID provider){% if not loop.last %}. {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Figures for these days are computed from the periods that were priced.</dd>
    {% endif %}
    <dt>Spread method</dt><dd>Best 1-hour spread is the mean of the two highest periods less the two lowest, within the same day. No cycling limits, degradation or round-trip losses applied.</dd>
    <dt>Status</dt><dd>Indicative market commentary. Not a basis for trading decisions and not an offer or recommendation.</dd>
  </dl>
</footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
